{"context":"The EKA direction treats Knowledge → Specification → Context → Reasoning → Execution as fundamental (fnd:llm-context-efficiency purpose). EKA already provides deterministic engineering context via contexts.Engine (ADR-021, depths local|dependency|engineering, bounded 64/2-hops, Entry refs 200B vs Document 2-4KB) and machine retrieval via eka get (ADR-015, --no-content/--compact/pagination). Despite this, agents over-fetch: domain dumps (100-300KB vs 5-15KB), file-level code (300 lines vs 40-line slice), raw tool outputs (5-50KB) and load-all skills/MCP schemas (30-37k prefix = 25-30% of 128k window) — the real budget killers per fnd §2. Research investigated 11 areas (1 Context Resolution via strata+role, 2 Progressive Disclosure L0-L6→existing filters, 3 Context Package=Context Object, 4 Unit/byte budget at EKA vs token at Agent, 5 Client-side ETag delta (no server session), 6 Code indexing, 7 Tool output filtering, 8 Tiered skill routing, 9 Instruction vs Knowledge separation P4/P5, 10 Reference-based \u003e summarization, 11 Four-way cache distinction) and validated via three spikes: spk:context-budget-knee (H1 knee ~5-12 units, strata-priority vs tail), spk:progressive-disclosure-latency (H4 L2-default + guardrail 8-10x saving, needs single-shot escape when neighbors\u003e4), spk:code-symbol-precision (symbol+1-hop import -72% tokens, p@1 +25pp, conditional GO, conditional RAG only as optional plugin). Current architecture must change what agents send to LLMs without new canonical schema or server state, preserving determinism (ADR-014 runtime consumer, P4 Protocol vs Content, P16 invariants) and model independence.","decision":"1. The Context Object (eka-context-v1, ADR-021) IS the Context Package. No second schema. Add objectHash to Entry (additive, cacheable by canonicalForm:objectHash:depth:optsHash), add thin filters --no-history / --only-section (alias --level) and document package = Context Object + dereference convention (refs → eka get on demand). Relevance = strata (\u003cfocus) + role (depends-on/derives-from) + type (adr/dec/std), never numeric score inside Engine.\n\n2. Progressive disclosure is FILTERING over deterministic object, not LLM summarization. Canonical instruction (replaces load-all): START eka context --depth dependency --no-content --compact (L2). Expand lazily via explicit eka get \u003clineForm\u003e only when role==constraint (stratum\u003cfocus) or role==depends-on for implementation; max 2 fetches sorted by lowest stratum then objectHash; NEVER fetch downstream unless audit; guardrail: if sections.constraints non-empty at L2 MUST expand minimal constraint set, else hallucinated contradiction. Single-shot escape: if estimated_neighbors_relevant\u003e4 OR turns_budget==1 use dependency full upfront (saves 1-2 RTT, measured E3). This is a skill-pack convention (eka-knowledge-retrieval), not Engine summarization.\n\n3. Budget is Agent Runtime advisory, not EKA token gate. EKA exposes unit/byte primitives (summary.units, summary.sections, --limit/--max-units, truncated:true envelope, bounded 64) deterministically sorted by canonicalForm. Agent Runtime enforces allocation (task 1k/constraints 2k/knowledge 3k/code 8k/evidence 2k est) via byte/4 heuristic, strata-priority keep: constraints \u003e dependencies \u003e decisions/planning \u003e downstream \u003e history (validated E1+E8). Never count tokens inside EKA (P4, model independence).\n\n4. Stateful delta lives CLIENT-SIDE (Agent Runtime cache), not server session. EKA provides content addressing (objectHash per CKO, snapshotDigest per repo, fileHash per code file) + Timeline.Line head check. Agent caches by objectHash (immutable forever) + byLine@instanceVersion (valid until Timeline bump) and uses If-None-Match style: send etag, server answers notModified or delta {addedEntries, removed, historyDelta}. No session table in EKA; prefix cache wins by freezing T0 (see 6).\n\n5. Tool output filtering belongs to Agent Runtime ToolOutputProcessor + pagination, not EKA core. EKA only paginates own tools (eka get --limit) and returns structured evidence {type, highlights[], hasMore:true, fullRef: tmp://...} with lazy read_output offset/limit. Per-tool extractors for git diff (changed_files/hunks), grep (file:line:preview top 20 by proximity to focus), test (failed_tests + first stacktrace), build logs. No LLM summarization of CKOs.\n\n6. Agent configuration tiered + capability routing via eka-router (existing 34-line router, now enforced): T0 Frozen Prefix always (~3-4k: minimal system prompt + thin AGENTS.md \u003c2k + eka-router ~0.8k, 100% prefix cacheable), T1 Capability-routed on demand (10 EKA skills 1.5-4k each via deterministic keyword table Task→Required Skill, not LLM), T2 Reference-via-EKA (knowledge via eka get, never baked into skills), T3 Grouped MCP (eka_read: get/context/view, eka_write: new/publish/transition, eka_ops: status/sync/validate, saves 50% schema tokens 6-12k→3-4k), T4 Removed (verbose examples → eka get std:\u003cid\u003e). SKILL.md must not contain concrete knowledge payloads (Instruction vs Knowledge separation P4/P5); knowledge lives in std-/gls- CKOs. Instruction version per EKA release, knowledge per publish.\n\n7. Compression hierarchy: structural dedup/canonicalization/metadata-first (Entry vs Document, --compact, dedup lineForm) = EKA deterministic (keep). LLM summarization = REJECT for knowledge/code (lossy, risks ADR paraphrase divergence); allowed only for unstructured tool logs with hasMore handle.\n\nAll changes additive, backward compatible; Engine remains Runtime consumer (runtime, exchange, conformance) without machine/view/store import, per ADR-021 §1.","consequences":"Positive: deterministic, bounded, reference-first context stays byte-identical per (subject,depth,optsHash) and cacheable (ETag objectHash); reclaim ~20k fixed prefix (T0 3-4k + routing vs 26k load-all) + 5-10x for ref-heavy contexts + ~72% for code tasks (-78% refs) as measured spk:code-symbol-precision; long sessions save 40-70% repeats via client delta without server state; provider prefix cache hit rate improves by separating instruction (quarterly) from knowledge (hourly). Negative: adds thin flags (--no-history/--only-section/--max-units, Entry.objectHash), Agent Runtime must implement Budget + ToolOutputProcessor + client cache (~2 weeks), skill pack needs audit (move excerpts to std-/gls-). Harness E1/E3/E8 still needs 3-5 days each to lock numeric knee (\u003e5-12) and expansion rate \u003e70% L2 sufficiency; if knee not at 5-12, budget defaults revised without schema change. Backward compat: new flags additive, old eka context/get unchanged, MCP grouping via alias preserves old tool names.","alternativesConsidered":"Rejected as primary: Generic RAG + vector search as primary context mechanism — non-deterministic, model-coupled, re-index cost per publish, precision ceiling for constraint tracing (strata invariant needs exact relationship not cosine); kept only as optional tooling-layer plugin for fuzzy code discovery (spk:code-symbol-precision fallback). Indiscriminate LLM summarization of CKOs — lossy, risks silent ADR divergence; kept only for tool logs with hasMore. Full repository context / load-all skills / blindly increasing context window (256k→1M) — O(repo) bloat, dilutes attention, 25% window burned fixed; replaced by bounded closure 32/64. Relevance scoring inside Engine — non-deterministic, invalidates cache, unproven vs strata/role filter on small graphs. Server-side session state — violates stateless EKA, stale constraint risk; replaced by client ETag cache. Full transitive call graph / AST dump to LLM — expensive, 30-40% incomplete in dynamic langs, token-inefficient; replaced by 1-hop name-match + fileHash cache + on-demand fetch. Token counting inside EKA — violates P4 + model independence; kept Agent-side byte/4 heuristic."}